    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Lean-SMT is a tactic to integrate the Lean Theorem Prover with cvc5, a Satisfiability Modulo Theory\r\n(SMT) solver. To increase automation in Lean, the tactic will reconstruct a proof of unsatisfiability\r\nproduced by cvc5 in Lean step by step. For successful proof reconstruction in Lean, every cvc5 proof\r\nrule and rewrite rule must already be a term in Lean’s library. Consequently, for cvc5’s bit-vector\r\nsolver, we formalize a theory of bit-vectors in Lean. This includes formalizing a novel bit-vector\r\nrepresentation, bit-blasting theorems, and bit-vector rewrite rules. We discuss the formalization\r\nprimarily and some challenges we faced.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Khan, M. (2024). Formalizing The Theory of Bit-vectors for Integration of SMT Solvers and Theorem Provers. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/nb615dd3764. https://doi.org/10.25740/nb615dd3764.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
